{
  "id": "RADAR-2025-0009",
  "category": "compromised-package",
  "title": "Shai-Hulud worm trojanises npm packages and publishes stolen secrets to GitHub",
  "summary": "A self-replicating payload named bundle.js was injected into @ctrl/tinycolor and, within days, roughly 500 other npm packages including CrowdStrike's; on install it downloaded TruffleHog, swept the host for npm, GitHub and cloud credentials, then used any valid npm token to republish the maintainer's own packages carrying the same payload. Stolen data was written to a public repository named Shai-Hulud in the victim's GitHub account and posted to a hardcoded webhook.site endpoint.",
  "indicators": [
